The attached image displays antibody titers against recombinant protective antigen (rPA) in mice, comparing the adjuvanticity of Nano-11 with aluminum hydroxide (AH). It shows that Nano-11, when co-administered with rPA, significantly enhances antigen-specific IgG titers across various doses (200, 50, and 12.5 µg) compared to rPA alone. Notably, at lower concentrations like 12.5 µg, Nano-11 demonstrates superior immunopotentiation compared to AH, which failed to induce a significant response at this dose. This highlights Nano-11's effectiveness as a vaccine adjuvant, even at low doses.